  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Hydrogen atom from excited state comes to the ground by emitting a photon of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. The value of principal quantum number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;of the excited state will be :</p><p>( <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Rydberg constant)</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When an electron jumps from a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;orbit to ground state, using Rydberg formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>In this case,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></math>. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
